name: gnomon-local
description: >-
  @a-company/gnomon-local — the local-model session child (spec §13.1), a
  separate executable driven by the kernel's #local-runner over stdio in pi's
  --mode rpc JSONL shape. Zero runtime deps; compat allowlist = llama.cpp,
  Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, mlx-lm (no cloud providers); loopback/LAN rule
  re-checked in the child; argument repair, text-tool fallback, tool surface
  none|compact|full, parallel tools, steer/follow_up queues. M1.8 slice 1.

components:
  gnomon-local:
    description: >-
      The gnomon-local child: src/endpoint.ts, compat.ts, client.ts (SSE
      streaming, no redirects), repair.ts, tools.ts (read_file, write_file,
      list_dir; confined to realpath roots cwd+worktree, writes never under .git or through a symlink final component), agent.ts (sticky abort; surface none never runs tools), rpc.ts, cli.ts (exitCode, never process.exit after writes); client byte caps + idle timeout. Slice 2: compaction.ts (re-derived; contextTarget
      ~8k from the session config; threshold compaction before a request that
      would not fit, one compact-and-retry on a context-overflow 400/413, a
      second overflow ends the run error; tool-less non-streamed summariser,
      reply normalised to exactly Goal/Constraints/Progress/Decisions/Next/
      Critical; history = system + summary + the longest safe tail within a
      quarter of the target, never an orphaned tool result; events
      compaction_start/_end; the summariser's usage is part of agent_end).
      Round 2 (M1): the summary escapes every < and sits in a block labelled model-generated / data-not-instructions; compaction_end carries summaryHash + summaryBytes. Round 2: history budget = 0.85 x target minus the native tools schema; at most one compaction per step (still over after it, or an overflow after it, ends the run with a clear error); the kept tail never starts at a text-tool <tool_result> message. Round 3: summary/tail caps derive from the budget; a config with maxTokens >= 0.85 x contextTarget is refused. Round 2: rpc steer is refused while the agent is idle (never queued into the next turn). Loops step 10 (#loop-act): protect.ts (the kernel's glob dialect, case-insensitive) and the session config's optional `tools` (the names the loop clamp admits; the agent offers and runs only those) and `protect` (repo-relative globs; write_file refuses a hit with a `protected-input:` result and no card, node_modules always); a malformed list is a ConfigError, never "all". Deferred: JSONL session tree, bash/edit tools.
    path: src/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, local, paradigm-8, m1.8]
    tests:
      - test/local-child.test.ts
      - test/compaction.test.ts
